        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "df97bd43-2976-3c88-82b6-bc4fa3723619",
                "word": "clownesque",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f8e2dc63-6ec3-45de-968d-289c5d7eca66",
                        "entry_id": "df97bd43-2976-3c88-82b6-bc4fa3723619",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "clownesques"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fce707cb-b48c-3f81-aee5-f0dc9c1bed05",
                        "entry_id": "df97bd43-2976-3c88-82b6-bc4fa3723619",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatif aux clowns."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2edce446-fa85-48a7-93b5-36664ba429d3",
                                "sense_id": "fce707cb-b48c-3f81-aee5-f0dc9c1bed05",
                                "text": "Bientôt, tous deux paraissaient dans l’arène, en tête du bataillon clownesque, vêtus de costumes à la fois singuliers et coquets, et Nello jetant, ma foi, en fort bon anglais au public la phrase consacrée des clowns :\n« Here we are again — all of a lump ! How are you ? »"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5bd1d09f-03dd-3532-8295-db4a92f13666",
                        "entry_id": "df97bd43-2976-3c88-82b6-bc4fa3723619",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui rappelle la drôlerie des clowns, leurs grimaces ou leurs maladresses."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae943f36-d21e-4b5b-9c86-b3b0e2e01e23",
                                "sense_id": "5bd1d09f-03dd-3532-8295-db4a92f13666",
                                "text": "A de telles époques, où peuvent trouver place les formidables goinfreries de gaieté du vieux Breughel ? Où le rire net et chantant de Jacques Callot ? Où la brutalité puissante d’Hogarth ? Où le débordement clownesque de Rowlandson ?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b39d5e50-9656-46e5-84c5-8eac468608ae",
                                "sense_id": "5bd1d09f-03dd-3532-8295-db4a92f13666",
                                "text": "Isaac a le corps mince et noueux, un visage entre Cassavetes et Belmondo à trente ans, l’expression clownesque."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "55c74499-b8ce-33d7-8c83-d835c53ca63c",
                        "entry_id": "df97bd43-2976-3c88-82b6-bc4fa3723619",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dont le ridicule fait penser aux clowns."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "pejorative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed029885-a136-4c88-9985-01ba21a944b2",
                                "sense_id": "55c74499-b8ce-33d7-8c83-d835c53ca63c",
                                "text": "Trompé par la gaucherie clownesque d'Achard, Jouvenel le tenait pour un demeuré :\n« Où est l'imbécile ? Appelez-moi l'imbécile ! »"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "36f5384d-f8e6-4fe4-b86e-8af066086df9",
                                "sense_id": "55c74499-b8ce-33d7-8c83-d835c53ca63c",
                                "text": "J’ai passé une heure à farfouiller dans mes archives vestimentaires pour dénicher une cravate clownesque d’avant la nationalisation des hydrocarbures."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e109bcb9-70f1-4623-933e-4f1bdf35cd58",
                        "source_entry_id": "df97bd43-2976-3c88-82b6-bc4fa3723619",
                        "target_lang_word": "clownish",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "clownish",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "759f923a-de2f-33d6-9193-6814212cd783",
                                        "entry_id": "6a3d4ff9-11e4-3f21-b931-e8eea8b3586d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Resembling or characteristic of a circus clown; comical, ridiculous."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "389af1a7-7ae4-421e-9353-1c83a85cf0c0",
                                                "sense_id": "759f923a-de2f-33d6-9193-6814212cd783",
                                                "text": "Even worse, the zombies' clownish makeup, with a stark white base and black shoe polish around the eyes, looks amateurish."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a746808-1742-4394-9db1-bd92d15cff54",
                                                "sense_id": "759f923a-de2f-33d6-9193-6814212cd783",
                                                "text": "Once again, City's defending was clownish. James McArthur drove into the area on the left and pulled a low cross towards the far post, where the horribly timid Gaël Clichy allowed Perch to bundle the ball past Costel Pantilimon."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86d28554-9d10-4fea-8544-57f087f09779",
                                                "sense_id": "759f923a-de2f-33d6-9193-6814212cd783",
                                                "text": "Indeed, when in close quarters to Rooney, it must prove almost irresistible to stick a plastic moustache and silly clownish shoes on the potato-headed fool."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4489d4cc-2015-3acc-8e80-69a56ea0e27b",
                                        "entry_id": "6a3d4ff9-11e4-3f21-b931-e8eea8b3586d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pertaining to peasants; rustic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "54f0786b-6e05-3156-a572-11bf6487f1d1",
                                        "entry_id": "6a3d4ff9-11e4-3f21-b931-e8eea8b3586d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Uncultured, boorish; rough, coarse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e230d3c-ff7f-4cea-a3ed-72cc196cd32b",
                                                "sense_id": "54f0786b-6e05-3156-a572-11bf6487f1d1",
                                                "text": "Large were his limbes, and terrible his looke, / And in his clownish hand a sharp bore speare he shooke."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8505ca64-c5e0-4079-b0b4-2c394bbfd0ed",
                                                "sense_id": "54f0786b-6e05-3156-a572-11bf6487f1d1",
                                                "text": "\"He is very plain, undoubtedly—remarkably plain:—but that is nothing compared with his entire want of gentility. I had no right to expect much, and I did not expect much; but I had no idea that he could be so very clownish, so totally without air. I had imagined him, I confess, a degree or two nearer gentility.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
